title: Hierarchical 4-State — Layerwise Viz and Inductive Bias Probes (2025-09-16)
tags: hierarchical_4_state, ebm, ar, visualization, ibp, layer_probe, tsne

## Overview
We study how an AR/EBM transformer encodes a 4-state hierarchical process. We:
- Generate hidden-state visualizations aligned to ground-truth states (including per-layer caches/plots).
- Run Inductive Bias Probes (IBP) with a linear probe on specific encoder layers to compare early vs final layer behavior.

Key takeaways:
- Early layer (layer 0) preserves causal-state structure better (higher D-IB, clearer separation on t-SNE).
- Final layer collapses toward next-bit decision (very high R-IB, low D-IB for many mappings), conflating distinct states with similar emissions.

