## Inductive Bias Probe (IBP) — layerwise probes
We compare probes on layer 0 vs final with identical settings on the same data/model.

Shared settings:
- `--preset custom` with provided `--states_data` (4-state labels)
- `--num_probe_datasets 20`, `--train_examples 1000`, `--val_examples 4000`, `--ft_steps 200`, `--ft_lr 1e-3`

Layer 0 probe:
```bash
MPLBACKEND=Agg uv run --with numpy --with torch \
  python3 experiments/ibp/ebm_ibp.py \
  --ckpt experiments/ebm/checkpoints/hierarchical_4_state_ebm.pt \
  --preset custom \
  --data experiments/datasets/hierarchical_4_state/hierarchical_4_state.dat \
  --states_data experiments/datasets/hierarchical_4_state/hierarchical_4_state.states.dat \
  --val_data experiments/datasets/hierarchical_4_state/hierarchical_4_state.dat \
  --val_states_data experiments/datasets/hierarchical_4_state/hierarchical_4_state.states.dat \
  --use_probe_head --probe_layer 0 \
  --num_probe_datasets 20 --train_examples 1000 --val_examples 4000 \
  --ft_steps 200 --ft_lr 1e-3 \
  --output experiments/ibp/results/h4_layer0_probe_full.json
```

Final layer probe:
```bash
MPLBACKEND=Agg uv run --with numpy --with torch \
  python3 experiments/ibp/ebm_ibp.py \
  --ckpt experiments/ebm/checkpoints/hierarchical_4_state_ebm.pt \
  --preset custom \
  --data experiments/datasets/hierarchical_4_state/hierarchical_4_state.dat \
  --states_data experiments/datasets/hierarchical_4_state/hierarchical_4_state.states.dat \
  --val_data experiments/datasets/hierarchical_4_state/hierarchical_4_state.dat \
  --val_states_data experiments/datasets/hierarchical_4_state/hierarchical_4_state.states.dat \
  --use_probe_head --probe_layer final \
  --num_probe_datasets 20 --train_examples 1000 --val_examples 4000 \
  --ft_steps 200 --ft_lr 1e-3 \
  --output experiments/ibp/results/h4_final_probe_full.json
```

## Results (summaries)
- Layer 0 probe (20 tasks):
  - R-IB ≈ 0.726 ± 0.084
  - D-IB ≈ 0.523 ± 0.070
  - File: `experiments/ibp/results/h4_layer0_probe_full.json`

- Final layer probe (same settings):
  - R-IB ≈ 0.908 ± 0.119
  - D-IB ≈ 0.220 ± 0.272 (many tasks with R-IB=1, D-IB=0)
  - File: `experiments/ibp/results/h4_final_probe_full.json`

Interpretation:
- Final layer aligns with next-token decision boundary (emission-centric), merging distinct states with similar p(next token).
- Early layer retains more causal-state identity (higher D-IB), consistent with per-layer t-SNE plots and centroid graph.

## Relation to IBP paper (attached as `experiments/ibp/paper.md`)
- Matches the paper’s finding: strong next-token performance does not imply inductive bias toward the full world model/state.
- Our layerwise result refines this: state is present early, then progressively coarsened toward emissions in later layers.
- Suggested follow-up (from paper): compute D-IB on next-token partitions (D-IB_{q=} vs D-IB_{q≠}) to directly test the “legal next-token” hypothesis in this binary setting.

## Suggested next steps
- Add a script to compute D-IB_{q=} / D-IB_{q≠} using our hierarchical states and the model’s legal-next-token partition.
- Export a side-by-side panel of per-layer t-SNE plots for the paper/notes.
- Optional: auxiliary head on layer 0 for state prediction (frozen backbone) to quantify linear decodability vs IBP behavior.

